Description: Wraps glm(), lme4::lmer(), and binomial glm() with a
    permutation loop to compute nonparametric p-values. For each model,
    ptestR generates a null distribution of the test statistic by randomly
    rearranging the outcome variable, then computes p.perm as the proportion
    of permuted statistics at least as extreme as the observed one. This
    approach requires far fewer distributional assumptions than standard
    Wald or likelihood-ratio tests, making it well-suited to neuroimaging,
    EEG, and other biomedical datasets with repeated measures and small
    samples.
